From 53566100a047beae2e2a30083705ef2cbceec5ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: noname <noname@example.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 02:41:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 36/36] Anchor a feature icon to its row, not to a parent that
 is briefly gone

Every rebuild of the label row logged

  DesktopGameLabels.qml:138: TypeError: Cannot read property
  'verticalCenter' of null

for each feature icon: a Repeater delegate has no parent for the moment between
the model change and the row taking it back, and the binding read the anchor
through that parent. Anchoring to the row by id gives the same layout without
the transient null, which is what patch 0002 already did for the launcher row.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [STM32MP25 performance work]
---
 opennow-qt/qml/desktop/components/DesktopGameLabels.qml | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/opennow-qt/qml/desktop/components/DesktopGameLabels.qml b/opennow-qt/qml/desktop/components/DesktopGameLabels.qml
index b15f2ea1..e37cce1e 100644
--- a/opennow-qt/qml/desktop/components/DesktopGameLabels.qml
+++ b/opennow-qt/qml/desktop/components/DesktopGameLabels.qml
@@ -135,7 +135,10 @@ Item {
                 Image {
                     required property int index
                     objectName: "desktopGameFeature-" + root.features[index]
-                    anchors.verticalCenter: parent.verticalCenter
+                    // Anchor to the row by id: a delegate is briefly parentless
+                    // while the model is rebuilt, and parent.verticalCenter then
+                    // logs a TypeError for every icon of every rebuild.
+                    anchors.verticalCenter: featureRow.verticalCenter
                     width: root.glyphSize
                     height: root.glyphSize
                     source: DesktopTokens.featureIconUrl(root.features[index])
